      "writtenOn": "2023-04-28T00:32:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, this was defined as a uint8_t slice in the vello_shaders crate to accommodate SPIR-V and other binary formats. I can certainly change the vello_shaders crate to return different types for different native shader source formats which can be cleanly expressed in Rust as an enum:\n\n\n    enum ShaderSource\u003c\u0027a\u003e {\n        Textual(\u0026\u0027a str),  // a string\n        Spirv(\u0026\u0027a [u32]),  // a slice of words\n        Binary(\u0026\u0027a [u8]),  // pre-compiled ISA\n    }\n\nThis gets annoying in C++ but I can imagine redefining `fSource` as a `std::variant` of various Span types or alternately adding different methods here like `nativeShaderSource`, `nativeShaderWords`, `nativeShaderSpirv` etc for the different formats.",
      "parentUuid": "78e42e10_56bec189",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "151ca77b9c5ea9769d937fb87c5fcf31bb6a5313",
